  "description": "<p>The import export utility should be able to export BagIt bags into a serialized format when they have a profile which specifies serialization is required. This should support zip, tar, and tar+gzip initially.</p>\n\n<p> </p>\n\n<p>Work can be done after \n    <span class=\"jira-issue-macro resolved\" data-jira-key=\"FCREPO-3205\" >\n                <a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-3205\" class=\"jira-issue-macro-key issue-link\"  title=\"Import serialized Bags\" >\n            <img class=\"icon\" src=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/universal_avatar/view/type/issuetype/avatar/10300?size=medium\" />\n            FCREPO-3205\n        </a>\n                                                    <span class=\"aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-subtle aui-lozenge-success jira-macro-single-issue-export-pdf\">Closed</span>\n            </span>\n as serializing a bag after the fact does not change the structure of the bag itself, so if it is required a user can currently do it after the fact.</p>",
